sents an athlete in contract negotiations"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Both sports agents and team owners are becoming more and more concerned with protecting their investments."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le15ob07aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pundit"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a knowledgeable person who gives an opinion on a particular subject"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Pundits questioned the decision to wear a mask."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le15ob07aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pioneer"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "someone who is one of the first people to do something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Over the years he has come to be seen as a pioneer."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le15ob07aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "trailblazing"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the first person to do something or go somewhere"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The effects of Plante's trailblazing decision are still being felt."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le15ob07aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "legendary"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very famous and admired"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He was a legendary goalkeeper for the Montreal Canadiens."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le15ob07aud07"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I create a list of important historical moments in a sport or competition."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I caption each moment with descriptive sentences."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share the information with a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose a sport or competition."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Chose at least five moments which were important in your sport's history."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In 5 panels, paste or draw an image of the moment and write a brief description."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Practice reading your sentences out loud."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Present your mini book of moments to a partner."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Passive: The Present Continuous and Present Perfect Tenses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Present Continuous to talk about an action that is happening at the time of speaking. The action or event is in progress. </br><span class=\"italic\"> People <span class=\"strong\">are </span>constantly<span class=\"strong\"> designing </span>new equipment.</span></br></br>You use the Present Perfect to talk about a finished action or event with present consequences. There is a connection between what happened in the past and the present. </br><span class=\"italic\">Players <span class=\"strong\">have worn</span> hockey masks since the 1950s.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You often choose the passive form when you want to talk about an action but are not so interested in saying who or what does/did it. Passives without <span class=\"italic\">agents</span> (the doers) are common in academic writing and biographies.  </br></br> Look at the chart below for the structure of the passive voice."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Name\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"am/are/is +  being + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">The effects of Plante's trailblazing decision <span class=\\\"strong\\\">are still being felt</span>.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"have/has + been + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Hockey masks <span class=\\\"strong\\\">have been worn</span> since the 1950s. </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Headgear has been improved upon by cricket batsmen, who wear not only a helmet but a faceguard."}, {"type": "example", "content": "In professional American football, full padding has been used for years, and new equipment is constantly being designed. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Hockey masks have been worn since the 1950s."}, {"type": "example", "content": "In an era when multimillion-dollar contracts are being handed out, both sports agents and team owners are becoming more and more concerned with protecting their investments. "}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about fame and work."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about social or urban change."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about what has been happening or what has been done."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What protective equipment is needed in your favorite sport?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Which famous athlete has changed sports the most?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_n