]}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn9le15ob07re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn9le15ob07re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn9le15ob07re2img01.jpg", "text": "", "id": 0}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn9le15ob07re2img01.jpg", "text": "Hockey masks have been worn since the 1950s. It was the legendary goalkeeper Jacques Plante who first entered a game wearing facial protection. On November 1, 1959, after having been struck by a hard shot, Plante retired to the dressing room. After the doctor had patched him up with stitches, the courageous Plante returned to the ice wearing a crude mask. At the time, Jacques Plante's unique style of dress was considered eccentric by reporters and pundits. Over the years, however, he has come to be seen as a pioneer.", "id": 1}, {"time": "34000", "image": "engenn9le15ob07re2img02.jpg", "text": "The effects of Plante's trailblazing decision are still being felt. In professional American football, full padding has been used for years, and new equipment is constantly being designed. In the minor leagues of hockey, full face masks are being worn on a trial basis, and in professional football, goalkeepers like Petr Cech are wearing small, padded helmets. Even rugby stars, who pride themselves on being the toughest of professional athletes, have begun to wear head protection. Headgear has been improved upon by cricket batsmen, who wear not only a helmet but a faceguard.", "id": 2}, {"time": "69500", "image": "engenn9le15ob07re2img03.jpg", "text": "It's no surprise that player safety has been a growing concern since Plante's day. In an era when multimillion-dollar contracts are being handed out, both sports agents and team owners are becoming more and more concerned with protecting their investments.", "id": 3}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": 